$ hibi -h
exit status: 0
---- standard output ----
Record that a statement was checked against evidence, and report what changed since

Usage: hibi [OPTIONS] <command>

Commands:
  init              Create the .hibi/ store in this git repository
  claim             Record a statement, what it is about and its evidence, as checked now
  status            Report which claims need a new check and why
  mark              Record that claims were checked again and still hold
  reanchor          Replace a claim with one that has a new statement, anchors or period
  retire            Retire claims that no longer apply
  cover             List the units in the declared scopes that no claim covers
  list              List stored claims, or show one claim with its history
  triage            Rank uncovered prose by how likely it states a checkable fact (judge)
  suggest-evidence  Rank code units that may be evidence for a statement (judge)
  providers         Show the built-in file provider, sibling repositories and schemes
  schema            Print the JSON Schema of a record, an input or a command's output
  completions       Print a shell completion script
  version           Print the hibi version

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help (see more with '--help')

Global options:
      --root <dir>       Use this directory as the root (the directory that contains .hibi/) instead of searching upward from the working directory
      --format <format>  Output format. Without this option the output is JSON when standard output is not a terminal, and text when it is [possible values: human, json]
      --now <timestamp>  Use this instant as the current time, for reproducible runs. RFC 3339 with any offset, for example 2026-11-20T18:04:11Z. A fraction of a second is dropped. The largest value is 9999-12-30T22:00:00Z
      --no-cache         Do not read or write the cache database. Every command that does not call the judge gives the same result with and without the cache. The judge commands (triage, suggest-evidence, status --judge-order) may rank differently from one run to the next without it
